WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.030
A restaurant group has vendors in
every corner. Toast at the counter,

2
00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:10.200
Sysco at the back door, Ecolab in the
dish room, Cintas for the linens.

3
00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:15.860
Connexcy keeps every agreement and invoice,
for every location, in one place,

4
00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:18.780
and pulls out the terms
that matter: prices,

5
00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:22.390
delivery minimums, renewal
dates and notice periods.

6
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:26.730
Your Cintas linen agreement renews
automatically for three more years,

7
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:29.010
unless you give notice 90 days ahead.

8
00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:32.940
Connexcy alerts your director
of operations six months out.

9
00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:37.440
Every invoice is matched to its agreement.
When a US Foods invoice charges

10
00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:42.530
a delivery fee your agreement waives,
it's flagged before anyone pays it.

11
00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.657
Before OpenTable renews, compare it
with other reservation platforms,

12
00:00:46.707 --> 00:00:50.030
and see why you chose it.
Then the general manager,

13
00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:54.493
the director of operations and
the owner sign off, in order.

14
00:00:55.103 --> 00:01:00.119
Connexcy for restaurants.
Every contract. Every invoice.

15
00:01:00.169 --> 00:01:03.156
Connected. Join the beta at connexcy.com.
